zink: keep freed buffers longer, as KGSL allocations are slow

KGSL zeroes and maps a buffer's pages when it is allocated, ~0.35 ms per
MiB on the Adreno 740 (6-8 ms for a 2800x1752 texture). KWin allocates
several such textures when a window is maximized or restored (the
cross-fade snapshot, the window's new texture, the upload's staging
buffer): with Zink's half-second cache each animation allocated them
again, 25-40 ms in its first frames, and dropped 3-5 frames at 120 Hz.
Keep freed buffers for a minute, at most 256 MiB of them.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c
@@ -1366,10 +1366,14 @@ zink_bo_init(struct zink_screen *screen)
    uint64_t total_mem = 0;
    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < screen->info.mem_props.memoryHeapCount; ++i)
       total_mem += screen->info.mem_props.memoryHeaps[i].size;
-   /* Create managers. */
+   /* Create managers. KGSL allocations are slow (~0.35 ms per MiB: the
+    * kernel zeroes and maps the pages): a compositor reallocating window
+    * textures on a resize or an animation dropped frames. Keep freed buffers
+    * for a minute, within a bound.
+    */
    pb_cache_init(&screen->pb.bo_cache, screen->info.mem_props.memoryTypeCount,
-                 500000, 1.5f, 0,
-                 total_mem / 8, offsetof(struct zink_bo, cache_entry), screen,
+                 60000000, 1.5f, 0,
+                 MIN2(total_mem / 8, 256 * 1024 * 1024), offsetof(struct zink_bo, cache_entry), screen,
                  (void*)bo_destroy, (void*)bo_can_reclaim);
 
    if (!pb_slabs_init(&screen->pb.bo_slabs,
